{"canManage() includes AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW in its permission check alongside AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE, meaning a principal that only has the view scope on the Groups resource type will pass the canManage() check - granting them the ability to create groups, update groups, add sub-groups, and map roles, all operations that should require manage scope": 0.9788109064102173, "groupResource.getId() returns the internal authorization resource UUID, not the group model ID, but hasPermission(String groupId, ...) looks up a resource via resourceStore.findByName(server, groupId) where the resource name is the group model ID - passing the internal UUID as if it were a name will always return null, causing the method to silently fall back to the all-groups resource policy check instead of evaluating per-group permissions": 0.9491302967071533, "getResourceName() is missing a handler for the new GROUPS resource type - for group resources, the method falls through to return resource.getDisplayName(), which returns the raw group UUID instead of a human-readable group name": 0.3835955262184143, "Double semicolon typo at the end of the field declaration for topGroup": 0.15960077941417694}